        "job": "Edit one document together with other people and AIs: edits merge in any order, words from different editors are kept, and undo takes back only my own edits",
        "description": "Give blocks (the document every editor started from: [{ id, text?, props? }] in order) and edits (one per editor, at most 6: { by, blocks }, the blocks that editor made their copy into; a new id is a new block, a block left out is removed). Each edit is turned into that editor's own operations by the document engine (do-work/document-operations.mjs: words as a sequence CRDT, block places and props as last-writer registers), the batches are merged in every order they could arrive in, and the merged document comes back with same_in_every_order and orders_checked. undo names one editor whose edit is then taken back: only what that editor inserted, deleted, moved or set, never words another editor added among them. Answers document ([{ id, text, props, format_version }], new blocks under the ids the engine mints), edits ([{ by, operations }]) and undone ({ by, operations }) when undo was given. Refuses no blocks or no edits, more than 6 editors, an editor named twice, an undo naming no editor here, and anything the engine refuses (with its code). Reads no records, keeps nothing after the run, and sends nothing: the live Write screen's page, saving to the person's records and the session sync are not part of this run.",
